WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.700
Start and controls
Take a seat and press Ready. The host starts when everyone is ready. Your cards or dice are at the bottom.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:19.000
Follow the turn prompt. Wait for animations to finish; an expired turn is played automatically. Use Return to room after settlement.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Gong Zhu | Highest total after four hands
Four players receive thirteen cards each, with no passing. Watch Demo N collect the sheep, avoid penalties and consider the transformer.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Club two opens each hand
Play clockwise. The highest card in the led suit collects all four cards and leads the next trick.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Follow suit or discard when void
Click a legal card on your turn. Follow the led suit whenever possible; otherwise discard any card.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:15.000
No trump, broken-hearts rule or first-trick penalty restriction. An ace outside the led suit cannot win.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:28.200
Rule note | Pig, sheep, hearts and transformer
Spade Q is −100 and diamond J +100. Hearts 2–4 score zero; 5–10 each −10; J/Q/K/A score −20/−30/−40/−50.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:39.000
Club ten doubles the other points. Alone, even with zero-point hearts, it scores +50. Exposed-card multipliers are not used.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:02:11.000
Complete the first thirteen tricks
Accelerate the remaining first-hand plays. Review captured scoring cards, hand points and cumulative totals. Each hand uses a fresh full deck.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:03:11.000
Accelerate hands two through four
Complete every remaining hand with the same following-suit rules. Scores accumulate across all four hands.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:22.000
Rule note | All hearts and grand slam
All thirteen hearts change the heart score from −200 to +200, doubled again if club ten is held.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:31.000
Capturing every heart, spade Q, diamond J and club ten instead scores exactly +1000, with no further doubling.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:49.000
Gong Zhu | Final four-hand totals
Highest cumulative score wins; ties are shared. Review each hand and its captures, then return to the room.
